# NEOCOM ecosystem tools

OpenSpec and Graphify are part of the NEOCOM workspace at the ecosystem root:

`neocom/` (parent of `neocom-meta`, `neocom-front`, `neocom-back`)

`neocom-meta` and `neocom-front` are git submodules of that parent; keep them synchronized via the parent's submodule pointers (`git submodule update --init --recursive`).

Agents should treat these as installed workspace tooling, not optional add-ons.

## OpenSpec

Spec-driven change workflow for AI coding tools. Docs: https://openspec.dev/docs/installation · https://openspec.dev/docs/cli

**Requires Node.js 20.19.0+.**

```bash
# Install CLI (once per machine)
npm install -g @fission-ai/openspec@latest

# Initialize at neocom root (Cursor)
cd /path/to/neocom
openspec init --tools cursor
```

After init, use the generated Cursor skills/commands (e.g. propose / apply / archive flows under the `opsx` or `openspec-*` names printed by init). Refresh with `openspec update` when the CLI upgrades.

## Graphify

Code-knowledge graph for Cursor. Package name is `graphifyy` (double y); CLI command is `graphify`.

```bash
# Install CLI (prefer uv)
uv tool install graphifyy
# alternatives: pipx install graphifyy  OR  pip install graphifyy

# Wire into Cursor at neocom root
cd /path/to/neocom
graphify install --platform cursor
graphify install --project --platform cursor

# Optional: build initial graph
graphify .
```

### Documentation / token maps from URLs

Graphify can fetch documentation URLs into a local corpus and build a knowledge graph (token / concept map):

```bash
cd neocom-meta/02.SOURCES
graphify add "https://example.com/docs" --dir raw
graphify .
graphify god-nodes --graph graphify-out/graph.json
graphify query "your question" --graph graphify-out/graph.json
```

Use this with the `extract-requirements-from-urls` skill and the catalog in `02.SOURCES/SOURCES.md`. Keep extracted human-readable requirements under `02.SOURCES/extracted/`.

## Agent guidance

- Prefer OpenSpec when the user wants a reviewable plan or change proposal before implementation.
- Prefer Graphify when navigating or explaining cross-folder structure and relationships under `neocom/`, and when mapping documentation corpora under `neocom-meta/02.SOURCES`.
- Prefer `/neocom-meta` + `extract-requirements-from-urls` when reading NestJS / EVE Online SSO sources for requirements.
- Prefer `/spec-collect` to turn `02.SOURCES` into L1 requirements; prefer `/spec-registration` to register atomic L1/L2 into OpenSpec.
- Do not re-install these tools on every task; only install or re-init when missing or when the user asks.
- Product code still belongs in `neocom-front` / `neocom-back`; agent config and docs in `neocom-meta`. Tool artifacts at the `neocom` root are shared ecosystem config.
